<div class="container">

<div class="book-title">
  <h1>Likutay Halachos</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Orach Chaim – Volume 1</div>
</div>

<div class="halacha-header">
  <h2>The Laws of Washing the Hands in the Morning — Halacha 1</h2>
</div>

<div class="sa-excerpt">
  <span class="sa-label">Shulchan Aruch, Orach Chaim 4</span>
  "When one rises, one should wash his hands," etc.
</div>

<p>See the discourse beginning "U'v'Yom HaBikurim" <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 56)</span>. For there is in every member of Israel an aspect of <i>Malchus</i>, etc. — see there.</p>

<p>For at night, the <i>Malchus</i> is in exile. For the essential completeness of the <i>Malchus</i> is through <span class="key"><i>arichus yamim</i></span> [length of days] — that is, the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>chasadim</i>. And at night, <i>dinim</i> overpower. And therefore, then the <i>da'as</i> is concealed. And therefore, the <i>Malchus</i> is diminished then and descends among the lower [realms]. For the essential <i>da'as</i> is received from the <span class="key">hands</span> — in the aspect of <i>machlokes l'shem Shamayim</i> [strife for the sake of Heaven] — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Let us lift up our hearts to our palms"</span> <span class="source">(Lamentations 3:41)</span> — etc. And at night, the pulsating spirit [<i>ru'ach hadofek</i>] does not blow so strongly, and the movement of the limbs is heavy at night. And on account of this, then sadness of spirit overpowers — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"In the evening, weeping shall lodge"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 30:6)</span>. And the essential overpowering is upon the hands, as explained there — the aspect of the sadness of the hands, etc.</p>

<p>And therefore, in the morning — when the spirit is renewed and all the limbs are recreated — then the sadness of spirit is nullified — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and in the morning, joy"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 30:6)</span>. And the pulsating spirit returns to flow properly through all the limbs — and the essential thing is in the hands. Therefore, one must purify specifically the hands — for there the sadness of spirit overpowered the most, as above. And conversely, now the holiness is drawn there the most. Therefore, one must sanctify and purify them. And the purification is with water — which is the aspect of <i>chasadim</i> — the aspect of <i>da'as</i>. And then, through this, one can <span class="key">build the <i>Malchus</i></span>. For the essential building of the <i>Malchus</i> is from the hands — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"His left hand is under my head, and his right hand"</span> <span class="source">(Song of Songs 2:6)</span> — etc. That is, through the pulsating spirit in the heart that is drawn to the hands, until one can lift them to the Heavens — and from there, one receives <i>diburim</i> [speech/words] in the aspect of <i>machlokes l'shem Shamayim</i>, as above. And this is the aspect of the <i>da'as</i>, through which the essential completeness of the <i>Malchus</i> comes, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the meaning of <span class="source">(Berachos 15a)</span>: "Whoever relieves himself, and washes his hands, and dons <i>tefillin</i>, and recites <i>Krias Shema</i> — it is as if he <span class="key">accepted the complete yoke of the Heavenly Kingdom</span>." For the essential completeness of the <i>Malchus</i> is through subjugating the evil and the <i>kelipos</i> that are attached to the holiness. And this is what our Rebbe wrote there: that the essential completeness of the <i>Malchus</i> is to reprove and to discipline the people — in order to expel the evil and the <i>kelipos</i>. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Remove the dross from the silver… remove the wicked from before the king, and his throne shall be established through <i>chesed</i>"</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 25:4–5)</span> — "through <i>chesed</i>" specifically. For through this, the <i>da'as</i> is drawn — which is the aspect of <i>chesed</i>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is why one must wash the hands <span class="key">twice</span>: before relieving oneself and afterward. For it is impossible to expel the evil except through the <i>da'as</i>, as explained there. And therefore, one must first purify the hands — in order to draw down <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of <i>arichus yamim</i>. And through this, one can reveal the concealment — that is, to expel and nullify the <i>kelipos</i> that conceal and hide the holiness. And from this itself is drawn <i>arichus yamim</i> — the aspect of <i>da'as</i> — as explained there. And this is the aspect of the second washing of the hands afterward — in order to draw down <i>da'as</i> and <i>arichus yamim</i> that one merits through expelling and clearing out the evil, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">donning of <i>tefillin</i></span> afterward. For through purifying the hands, one can then lift them — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"when I lift up My hands to the Heavens"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 32:40)</span> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"lift up your hands in holiness"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 134:2)</span>. And <i>da'as</i> is drawn from the hands into the <i>mochin</i>, as above. And from this comes the aspect of <i>tefillin</i>, which are <i>mochin</i> — and they are the aspect of life and <i>arichus yamim</i> — as our Sages said <span class="source">(Menachos 44a)</span>: "Whoever dons <i>tefillin</i> merits long life."</p>

<p>And this is the meaning of: <span class="verse">"Who shall ascend the mountain of Hashem, and who shall stand in His holy place?"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 24:3)</span>. That is, who can merit <i>da'as</i> — which is the aspect of the mountain of Hashem and His holy place — that is, the <i>Beis HaMikdash</i> — which is the aspect of <i>da'as</i>? <span class="verse">"He who has clean hands and a pure heart"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 24:4)</span>. For through a pure heart, he has clean hands — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Let us lift up our hearts to our palms"</span> <span class="source">(Lamentations 3:41)</span>. And through this, he can ascend the mountain of Hashem — to merit <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of: "when I lift up My hands to the Heavens" — the aspect of <i>machlokes l'shem Shamayim</i>, as above. And this is the aspect of <i>Chesed</i>, <i>Gevurah</i>, <i>Tiferes</i> — which ascend and become <i>Chochmah</i>, <i>Binah</i>, <i>Da'as</i>.</p>

<p>And this is what is written in the <i>Shulchan Aruch</i> <span class="source">(Orach Chaim 4:3)</span>: that it is forbidden to touch, before the washing, the mouth, the nose, the eyes, and the ears — which are the aspect of the <span class="key">seven lights</span> that receive the light of the Face — that is, the intellect. And the receiving is from the hands. And when the hands are impure, one can receive the opposite, G-d forbid — since their receiving is from the hands, as above.</p>

<p>And afterward, one recites <i>Krias Shema</i> — which is the acceptance of the yoke of the Heavenly Kingdom — which one merits through having relieved himself, washed his hands, and donned <i>tefillin</i>, as above. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">revelation of the concealment</span> — as it is written: <span class="verse">"Hashem is our G-d, Hashem is One"</span> — that even in all the concealments, everything receives its life-force from Him, and <span class="aramaic">"there is no place void of Him."</span></p>

<p>And this is what is written in the Holy <i>Zohar</i> <span class="source">(<i>Eikev</i> 273a)</span>: one must lengthen the <i>dalet</i> of <i>echad</i> — as it is written: <span class="verse">"in order that he may prolong his days upon his kingdom"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 17:20)</span>. That is, as above: the essential <i>Krias Shema</i> — which is the <i>dalet</i> of <i>echad</i> — is the aspect of drawing <i>arichus yamim</i>, which is the <i>da'as</i>, into the <i>Malchus</i>.</p>

<p>And this is what our Sages said <span class="source">(Berachos 15a)</span>: "Whoever relieves himself, and washes his hands, and dons <i>tefillin</i>, and recites <i>Krias Shema</i> — it is as if he accepted the complete yoke of the Heavenly Kingdom." For all of this is the aspect of the completeness of the <i>Malchus</i>, as above. And this is what our Sages said — and they conclude there — that it is also considered as if he <span class="key">immersed</span>. For this is the aspect of immersion — the aspect of <i>mikveh</i> — the aspect of the supernal <i>da'as</i> and great <i>chasadim</i> — which is the essential completeness of the <i>Malchus</i>, as above — as explained there. See there. Examine well the Torah-teaching "U'v'Yom HaBikurim" mentioned above, and you will understand these words. For all this was written in brief, and it is impossible to understand the words well except after studying the Torah-teaching mentioned above.</p>

<div class="halacha-header">
  <h2>The Laws of Washing the Hands in the Morning — Halacha 2</h2>
</div>

<div class="sa-excerpt">
  <span class="sa-label">Introduction</span>
  The matter of washing the hands in the morning when one awakens from his sleep — based on what our Rebbe, of blessed memory, said in <i>siman</i> 250 regarding the question of that necromancer <span class="source">(Berachos 59a)</span>: "What is an earthquake?" — "When the Holy One, blessed be He, remembers His children who dwell in suffering among the nations, He drops two tears into the Great Sea, and the sound is heard from one end of the world to the other" — see there. For all the sufferings that a person has, G-d forbid, are only from the lack of <i>da'as</i>. For whoever has <i>da'as</i> and knows that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> has no sufferings and feels no distress, etc. And the essential distress of Israel in exile is only because they have fallen from <i>da'as</i> and attribute things to nature and <i>mazal</i>, G-d forbid. And this is because they dwell among the nations and have learned from them, etc. And in truth, Israel is above nature, but when they sin, G-d forbid, then, etc. And when the Holy One, blessed be He, wishes to save Israel from their exile, He draws upon them <i>hashgachah</i> from the ends of the world. For in the Future, He will nullify nature entirely and there will be only <i>hashgachah</i> alone — as it is written: <span class="verse">"For the heavens shall vanish like smoke"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 51:6)</span> — etc. — that is, that nature shall be nullified, which operates according to the arrangement of the constellations, etc. And then Israel shall be above. And therefore, even now, when Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> wishes to bring down the nations and to elevate Israel above — He draws upon them <i>hashgachah</i> from the ends of the world, where there will be only <i>hashgachah</i>. And through this <i>hashgachah</i>, Israel is elevated — and it becomes, etc. — see there all this well.
</div>

<span class="ois">§1</span>

<p>And when the <i>da'as</i> mentioned above departs — that is, when one does not know, G-d forbid, that everything is conducted only through <i>hashgachah</i> from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> alone, and one thinks there is nature, G-d forbid — this is the aspect of <span class="key">sleep, which is the departure of <i>da'as</i></span> — the aspect of night and darkness. For the essential light and day is the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, as is brought. That is, the light is only Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as it were — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Hashem is my light and my salvation"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 27:1)</span> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"G-d, Hashem, and He has given us light"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 118:27)</span>. And this is the essential light of the sun — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"For Hashem <i>Tzevakos</i> is a sun and a shield"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 84:12)</span>. That is, when one knows that Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> conducts the world through <i>hashgachah</i> alone — this is the essential light. For the essential light — wherever light is found, such as the light of the sun and the like — it is only the light of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as it were, Who illuminates for us, as above. And when one falls, G-d forbid, from this <i>da'as</i> and attributes things to nature, G-d forbid — this is the aspect of the departure of the light. And then it is the aspect of night and darkness, G-d forbid. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the sun darkened in its going forth"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 13:10)</span> — etc. — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"sun and moon became dark"</span> <span class="source">(Joel 2:10)</span> — etc. And similar such verses — all said regarding the time of exile. That is, in the exile it is considered as if the light of the sun is darkened — for the exile is compared to night, as explained in the commentary of Rashi. That is, in the time of exile — which is drawn only from the fact that people attribute things to nature, G-d forbid — then "the sun darkened in its going forth." For as soon as one attributes things to nature, G-d forbid, the light is removed from the sun, as if the sun itself is actually darkened. For in truth, the sun has no light at all except from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as above. And therefore, the exile is compared to night and darkness. For the essential exile is only because people attribute things to nature, G-d forbid — and then it is the aspect of night and darkness — the departure of light, as above. And this is the aspect of sleep — the departure of the <i>da'as</i> to know that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the essential light, etc. — as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, during sleep, the <span class="aramaic"><i>sitra d'mesaava</i></span> [impure side] rests upon a person — and primarily upon the <span class="key">hands</span> — as is written in the Holy <i>Zohar</i> <span class="source">(<i>Vayeishev</i> 184b)</span>. For the essential <i>sitra achra</i> — which is the aspect of the idolatrous nations, as is known — their nourishment is only from the aspect of <i>kefiros</i> — which is the essential root of the evil inclination, which is called <span class="aramaic">"another god" — <i>kefiros</i></span>, as is brought. That is, when people attribute things to nature, G-d forbid — from there is the essential nourishment of the nations and the <i>sitra achra</i>. And therefore, during sleep — the departure of the <i>da'as</i>, as above — then the aspect of the nations overpowers, G-d forbid — the aspect of the intensity of the exile that is compared to night and sleep — whose nourishment is from the aspect of the overpowering of nature, as above. And this is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">"the impure side that rests upon a person"</span> [during sleep].</p>

<p>And therefore, the essential rectification of sleep in holiness is through <span class="key"><i>emunah</i></span>, as is brought in the words of our Rebbe, of blessed memory <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 35)</span>. That is, during the departure of the <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of sleep — that is, when a person sees that his mind is confused and not in completeness, and he cannot know and understand that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> alone — like now in the exile among the nations, which resembles night and darkness, when the wisdom of nature overpowers in the world, G-d forbid — then every member of Israel is obligated to cast aside and remove his <i>da'as</i> entirely, and to strengthen himself with <i>emunah</i> alone: to believe with complete <i>emunah</i> that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> alone, and there is no nature in the world at all.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the rectification of sleep through <i>emunah</i>. That is, during sleep, as above, one must enter into the aspect of <i>emunah</i> — to rely on <i>emunah</i> alone — since the <i>da'as</i> has departed — like now in the exile, when we must constantly strengthen ourselves with <i>emunah</i> alone, since the <i>da'as</i> has not yet been fully revealed — to know in truth that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i>. Therefore, one must remove his <i>da'as</i> and rely on <i>emunah</i> alone — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and Your faithfulness in the nights"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 92:3)</span>.</p>

<p>And because at night, during sleep — the departure of <i>da'as</i> — the wisdom of nature overpowers, G-d forbid — which is the aspect of darkness, as above — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and a deep sleep fell upon Avram, and behold, a fear, a great darkness"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 15:12)</span> — which showed him the intensity of the exile. That is, during sleep and deep slumber — the departure of <i>da'as</i> — the intensity of the exiles overpowers, whose nourishment is from the aspect of the overpowering of nature, as above. And this is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">"the impure side that rests upon a person during sleep,"</span> as above.</p>

<p>Therefore, immediately when one awakens from his sleep, one must wash his hands in water. For the essential impure side rests upon a person's hands, as is written in the Holy <i>Zohar</i> (ibid.). For the hands are the aspect of <i>shamayim</i> [Heavens] — fire and water — the right hand and the left hand — the aspect of: "when I lift up My hands to the Heavens" — as is brought in the words of our Rebbe in another place <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 56)</span>. And there is the essential hold of the <i>sitra achra</i> — the aspect of the wisdom of nature — in the aspect of "hands." For they attribute things to the arrangement of the Heavens, which is the aspect of "hands." And therefore, the essential overpowering of the <i>sitra achra</i> during sleep — which is the aspect of nature — is in the hands specifically, as above. For the hands are <span class="key">28 joints</span> [<i>pirkei</i>], corresponding to the 28 letters in the account of Creation, through which the Heavens and earth were created — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Indeed, My hand has founded the earth, and My right hand has spread out the Heavens"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 48:13)</span>.</p>

<p>And therefore, the essential subjugation of the <i>sitra achra</i> — which is the idolatrous nations of the world — the aspect of the wisdom of nature from which they draw their power, as above — their essential subjugation is only through the <span class="key">hands of holiness</span>, when one merits to raise them to the <i>da'as</i>. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And it was, when Moshe would raise his hand, Israel prevailed; and when he would rest his hand"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 17:11)</span> — etc. — said regarding the war with Amalek. For Amalek is the totality of all the nations and the <i>sitra achra</i> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the first of the nations is Amalek"</span> <span class="source">(Numbers 24:20)</span>. And Amalek was a heretic who denied the essence and attributed everything to nature, G-d forbid — and they would calculate the hours through their astrology, as is brought in the commentary of Rashi, and as is brought in the words of our Rebbe, of blessed memory. And therefore, the essential subjugation of [Amalek] is through the raising of the hands — that one raises the hands, the 28 joints of the hands, to the head — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Lift up your hands in holiness"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 134:2)</span>. That is, one elevates the hands — the 28 joints — to the <i>da'as</i>: to know that everything is through His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i>. For Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> created everything through the 28 letters of the account of Creation, which are the aspect of the 28 joints, as above. And then one elevates the aspect of the Heavens — which are also the aspect of "hands," as above — to their root in the <i>da'as</i> — to the aspect of the 28 letters mentioned above. For Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> created everything through the 28 letters, and He vivifies and sustains the Heavens and all their host and the earth, etc. — through His <i>hashgachah</i> alone. And there is no nature or arrangement of the Heavens at all. And then Amalek and the <i>sitra achra</i> are subdued, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and his hands were <i>emunah</i> until the sun set"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 17:12)</span>. For the essential subjugation of Amalek is through <i>emunah</i> in the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> — which is drawn through the raising of the hands, as above. And therefore, during sleep — the departure of <i>da'as</i> — when it is the aspect of the overpowering of nature, G-d forbid — and then the <i>sitra achra</i> rests upon a person — therefore, the essential hold is in the hands, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, immediately when one awakens from sleep, one must <span class="key">wash his hands in water</span> — which is the aspect of the waters of <i>da'as</i>, the waters of <i>chesed</i> — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 11:9)</span>. That is, through the washing, one draws pure waters — waters of <i>da'as</i> — from the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> [the World to Come], where the earth shall be full of <i>da'as</i> like the waters cover the sea, etc. And then all will know that everything is only through <i>hashgachah</i> alone, for nature will be completely nullified. And also now, at every time when one needs salvation and purification — to be saved from the intensity of the <i>sitra achra</i>, whose nourishment is from the aspect of the wisdom of nature — then one draws <i>hashgachah</i> from the ends of the world, as above in the discourse mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the waters of the washing — that one draws waters of <i>da'as</i> from the ends of the world, from the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, where the earth shall be full of <i>da'as</i>, etc. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key"><i>mikveh</i></span>, which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, as is known (for <i>mikveh</i> has the numerical value of 151, the aspect of <i>Binah</i> — <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — as is brought) — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the <i>mikveh</i> of Israel is Hashem, Who saves him in time of trouble"</span> <span class="source">(Jeremiah 14:8)</span>. For all the troubles and sufferings are only from the lack of <i>da'as</i>, from the aspect of the wisdom of nature, as above — that is, that one does not know, G-d forbid, that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i>, etc. And this is the essential <i>tumah</i> [impurity], as above. And therefore, the salvation from the trouble and the purification from the <i>tumah</i> is through the <i>mikveh</i> — which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — the aspect of the waters of <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of: "for the earth shall be full of <i>da'as</i> like the waters," etc. For through entering the <i>mikveh</i> and closing one's eyes from the sight of this world, and being concealed and covered there within the waters of the <i>mikveh</i> — which is the aspect of the waters of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — through this, one is encompassed within the aspect of the <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. For he closes his eyes from the sight of this world, where the error of the wisdom of nature overpowers — from which come all the troubles and all the impurities — through which the eyes are blemished, whose root and life-force is from the aspect of the "eyes of Hashem" — which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>, as understood from the discourse mentioned above. And when one falls from the <i>da'as</i> and thinks there is nature, G-d forbid — this is the aspect of the blemish of the eyes. And from this come all the troubles, etc. — as above. And therefore, one must close one's eyes entirely from the sight of this world, and be concealed and encompassed within the <i>mikveh</i> — which is the aspect of the <i>da'as</i> of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — when His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> will be revealed in the world and nature will be completely nullified. And through this, one draws <i>hashgachah</i> from the ends of the world, from the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>. And through this, salvation comes for whatever one needs — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the <i>mikveh</i> of Israel is Hashem, Who saves him in time of trouble,"</span> etc.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">morning washing</span>: that one draws pure waters drawn from the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>. And through this, one purifies his hands — which are the aspect of the 28 joints, the aspect of the 28 letters of the account of Creation. For the essential blemish of the aspect of the wisdom of nature — which overpowers during sleep, in the night and darkness — affects them specifically, as above. For through the wisdom of nature, one blemishes the 28 letters mentioned above and attributes things to the arrangement of the Heavens, G-d forbid — as above. And this is the aspect of the <i>tumah</i> that takes hold of the hands specifically during the departure of <i>da'as</i> — that is, during sleep — as above. And therefore, one purifies them through the waters of <i>da'as</i>, drawn from the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, etc. — as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§2</span>

<p>And therefore, before the washing, it is forbidden to touch with one's hands the <span class="key">seven openings</span> in the head — that is, the two eyes, the two nostrils, the mouth, and the two ears <span class="source">(Shulchan Aruch, Orach Chaim 4:3)</span>. For these seven openings are the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, as is brought in the words of our Rebbe in another place <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 21)</span>. And these seven openings of the head are in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"these seven are the eyes of Hashem, ranging over all the earth"</span> <span class="source">(Zechariah 4:10)</span> — the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. And therefore, it is forbidden to touch them with one's hands before the washing — so as not to blemish the holy <i>da'as</i> of the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> through the contamination of the wisdom of nature that clings to the hands during sleep, as above. And therefore, the essential dominion of the wisdom of nature — where they look only at the arrangement of the Heavens — is at night. For they are called "stargazers." For the wisdom of nature is the aspect of night and darkness — for the essential light is only the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> alone, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§3</span>

<p>And therefore, one must <span class="key">rise at midnight</span> — to break the sleep — to break the aspect of darkness and night — which is the aspect of the intensity of the exile that is compared to night — that is, the wisdom of nature, from which is the essential exile and darkness, as above. And every member of Israel must awaken from sleep at <i>chatzos</i> — in order to break and nullify the wisdom of nature, through breaking the sleep, etc. — as above. And therefore, when one rises at <i>chatzos</i>, one then mourns over the exile — that Israel was exiled from their land. For the essential exile is through the wisdom of nature, which is the aspect of night and sleep, as above. And therefore, that is the time to rectify this.</p>

<span class="ois">§4</span>

<p>And therefore, the <span class="key">first redemption</span> — which is the Exodus from Egypt, which encompasses all the redemptions (for all the exiles are referred to by the name "Egypt," as our Rebbe wrote in another place <span class="source">[Likutay Moharan I, 4]</span>) — therefore the redemption began at midnight — as it is written: <span class="verse">"At about midnight, I will go out in the midst of Egypt"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 11:4)</span>. For the essential of all the redemptions — in particular the redemption from Egypt — was through the aspect mentioned above in the discourse mentioned above: through the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> that Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> drew from the ends of the world, from <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>. For then, at the Exodus from Egypt, there was an overturning of the constellations and a nullification of nature. For then Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> revealed His <i>hashgachah</i> through the awesome wonders He performed then, and nullified nature. And all this was through the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — for <span class="aramaic">"from the side of <i>Yovel</i> they went out"</span> — which is the aspect of the fifty gates of <i>Binah</i>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, as is known.</p>

<p>And therefore, the redemption was at midnight specifically — that is, He broke the night and the darkness, which are the aspect of the wisdom of nature — and revealed <i>hashgachah</i> in the world. And through this was the essential redemption, as above. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and every firstborn in the land of Egypt shall die"</span> — <span class="verse">"and Hashem passed over"</span> — etc. — and He saved the firstborn of Israel. For <span class="key">"firstborn"</span> is "the beginning" — the aspect of <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the beginning of knowledge"</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 1:7)</span>. That is, He subdued the <i>da'as</i> of the <i>sitra achra</i> — which is the aspect of the wisdom of nature — and He strengthened the <i>da'as</i> of holiness — the aspect of the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"My son, my firstborn, is Israel"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 4:22)</span>. That is, the <i>da'as</i> of faith in <i>hashgachah</i> — from which is drawn the holy seed of Israel. For Israel is above nature, as above. For they are drawn from there — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Look now toward the heavens and count the stars… so shall your seed be"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 15:5)</span>. And our Sages expounded <span class="source">(Midrash Rabbah ad loc.)</span> that He raised him above the heavens, etc. It emerges that the seed of Israel is drawn from above nature — for according to nature, according to the arrangement of the heavens, Avraham Avinu, peace be upon him, was not fit to father children. Only through Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> telling him: "Go out from your astrology" — and raising him above the heavens — that is, above nature — through this, he merited to father children — the aspect of: "so shall your seed be." It emerges that the seed of Israel is drawn, in their root, from the aspect of above nature. And this is the aspect of the "firstborn of Israel" that Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> saved, and He slew the firstborn of Egypt at midnight — to subdue and break and nullify the <i>da'as</i> of the wisdom of nature, and to strengthen the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the aspect of the firstborn of the children of Israel, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§5</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And he divided against them"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 14:15)</span> — said regarding Avraham when he pursued the kings. For <span class="key">Avraham revealed the <i>hashgachah</i></span> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> in the world. And therefore, the essential sustaining of the generations of the heavens and the earth is through Avraham — as it is written: <span class="verse">"These are the generations of the heavens and the earth when they were created [<i>b'hibar'am</i>]"</span> — [read as] <i>b'Avraham</i> <span class="source">(Bereishis Rabbah ad loc.)</span>. For he revealed the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> in the world — through which the essential sustaining of the world comes. And therefore, Avraham had the power to divide the night — that is, to break the night — which is the aspect of the nullification of nature — the aspect of <i>kimas chatzos</i>, as above. And then he subdued the four kings — which are the aspect of the four kingdoms, as is brought.</p>

<p>For the essential subjugation of [the nations] is through the nullification of nature, as above. And therefore, because he blemished [his faith] through saying: <span class="verse">"By what shall I know that I shall inherit it?"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 15:8)</span> — the exile was decreed on account of this. For he blemished the <i>da'as</i>, which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — for the essential <i>da'as</i> is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. And <i>hashgachah</i> is the aspect of <i>Eretz Yisrael</i> — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the eyes of Hashem your G-d are always upon it"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 11:12)</span> — as our Rebbe wrote in another place. And therefore, through blemishing the <i>da'as</i> and blemishing <i>Eretz Yisrael</i>, which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — through this: <span class="verse">"and a deep sleep fell upon Avram, and behold, a fear, a great darkness falling upon him"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 15:12)</span> — which showed him the intensity of the exiles — which are the aspect of deep slumber, the aspect of darkness — whose essential overpowering is through the wisdom of nature — through the blemish of <i>hashgachah</i>, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§6</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key">eating <i>matzah</i> and the prohibition of <i>chametz</i></span>. For <i>matzah</i> is the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>mochin d'gadlus</i> [mature intellect], the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the essential <i>da'as</i>. And <i>chametz</i> is the aspect of <i>mochin d'katnus</i> [immature intellect], the aspect of <i>Elokim</i>, the aspect of <i>dinim</i>, as is brought in the <i>kavanos</i>. This is the aspect of the wisdom of nature — from which is the essential source of <i>dinim</i> and troubles, G-d forbid, as above. For <i>hateva</i> [nature] has the same numerical value as <i>Elokim</i>, as is brought — from which is the hold of the <i>dinim</i>, as above. For <i>chametz</i> is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"when my heart was <i>embittered</i> [<i>yischametz</i>]"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 73:21)</span> — etc. — which is said regarding the <i>kushyos</i> [difficult questions] that fall upon a person regarding the conduct of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> — which is the aspect of the wisdom of nature, from which come all the heresies and the <i>kushyos</i>.</p>

<p>But <i>matzah</i> is the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>emunas hahashgachah</i> [faith in Providence] — which is the essential <i>da'as</i>, as above. For <i>matzah</i> is on account of the fact that they went out in haste and the dough of our fathers did not have time to rise, until the King of kings, the Holy One, blessed be He, revealed Himself to them and redeemed them — as it is written: <span class="verse">"And they baked the dough that they had brought out of Egypt into cakes of <i>matzah</i>, for it had not risen, for they were driven out of Egypt and could not delay, and they had not even prepared provisions for themselves"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 12:39)</span>. For they had <i>emunah</i> in the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> — and therefore they did not prepare any provisions, and they went out in <span class="key">haste</span>.</p>

<p>It emerges that <i>matzah</i> is the aspect of the <i>da'as</i> of <i>emunas hahashgachah</i> — which is the essential greatness of <i>da'as</i>: when one merits the revelation of G-dliness — to see and know that everything is through His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> alone. And this is the aspect of haste — for haste is the aspect of above time — that He leaped over the end and took them out in great haste, without any time — but in a single moment and in a brief hour, they came from Ra'amses to Sukkos and were gathered together in a brief hour — six hundred thousand from the entire land of Egypt — as Rashi explained on the verse: <span class="verse">"and I bore you on eagles' wings"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 19:4)</span>. All of this is the aspect of above time. That is, He raised them above time — which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>, which is above nature, above time. And through this, they went out without any time, without any preparation — but in a brief hour — for the essential redemption was through the revelation of the <i>hashgachah</i>, which is above time — the aspect of haste.</p>

<p>For haste is the aspect of <i>zerizus</i> [alacrity] — which is a very good trait — the aspect of <i>emunah</i> — the aspect of the breaking of sleep that comes through laziness — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"laziness casts into a deep sleep"</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 19:15)</span> — and as is brought in another place in the words of our Rebbe: that <i>zerizus</i> is the aspect of <i>emunah</i> — see there. And this is the aspect of <span class="key"><i>zikaron</i></span> [remembrance] — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Remember this day, on which you went out of Egypt"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 13:3)</span> — etc. — and as it is written: <span class="verse">"in order that you shall remember the day you went out of the land of Egypt all the days of your life"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 16:3)</span> — etc. For it is stated in the words of our Rebbe, at the end of the discourse "V'Eileh HaMishpatim" — which speaks of <i>emunah</i> — <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 7)</span>: that <i>zikaron</i> is the aspect of <i>emunah</i>. For the essential <i>shich'chah</i> [forgetfulness] is from the aspect of time, etc. And when one knows and believes in truth that everything is conducted only according to the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> alone — Who is above time — then there is no aspect of forgetfulness at all, etc. — see there and understand. And this is the aspect of <i>zikaron</i> that is said in connection with the Exodus from Egypt — the aspect of: "Remember this day," etc. — "in order that you shall remember," etc. For at the Exodus from Egypt, His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> was revealed, as above — which is the aspect of <i>zikaron</i> — above time — above nature — the aspect of haste — the aspect of <i>zerizus</i>, which vivifies the <i>mochin</i> and the <i>da'as</i>, whose essential sustaining is when one knows and believes in the <i>hashgachah</i>. And this is the aspect of <i>matzah</i> — on account of the haste, etc. — etc. — as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§7</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key"><i>Shabbos HaGadol</i></span> — that the <i>Shabbos</i> before <i>Pesach</i> is called <i>Shabbos HaGadol</i> — on account of the miracle, etc. For the essential miracles and wonders that occurred at the Exodus from Egypt — that He overturned the constellations and nullified nature and revealed His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> in the world — all was drawn from the aspect of <i>Shabbos</i>, which is <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — "which is entirely <i>Shabbos</i>." From there, Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as it were, draws the <i>hashgachah</i> from the aspect of the end of the world, etc. — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the end has come; the end"</span> — etc. — as explained there in the discourse mentioned above. It emerges that the essential Exodus from Egypt was drawn from the aspect of <i>Shabbos</i>, which is the aspect of the World to Come. And therefore, <i>Pesach</i> too is called "<i>Shabbos</i>" — as it is written: <span class="verse">"And you shall count for yourselves from the day after the <i>Shabbos</i>"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 23:15)</span> — meaning <i>Pesach</i>, as our Sages said <span class="source">(Menachos 65b)</span>. For the essential intensity of the miracle of <i>Pesach</i> is drawn from <i>Shabbos</i>, as above. And this is the aspect of the <i>Shabbos</i> before <i>Pesach</i>, which is called <i>Shabbos HaGadol</i> on account of the miracle — for all the miracles of the Exodus from Egypt were drawn from the aspect of <i>Shabbos</i>, as above. And therefore, it is called "gadol" [great] — on account of the miracles, which are called the aspect of "great" — as it is written: <span class="verse">"Tell me the great things that Elisha did"</span> <span class="source">(II Kings 8:4)</span> — as our Rebbe wrote there in the discourse mentioned above, on the statement: "and He drops two tears into the Great Sea" — see there.</p>

<span class="ois">§8</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="source">(Pesachim 2a)</span>: <span class="key">"On the night [<i>or</i>] of the fourteenth, one searches for <i>chametz</i> by the light of the candle"</span> — and the Tanna called the night "<i>or</i>" [light] — in a refined expression, etc. For the essential searching for and removal of <i>chametz</i> is the aspect of the removal of the aspect of nature from the world — which is the aspect of <i>chametz</i>, as above. And when nature is nullified and <i>hashgachah</i> is revealed — this is the aspect of the nullification of darkness and night, as above — which are the aspect of the intensity of the exiles, drawn from the aspect of the wisdom of nature, as above. For when His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> is revealed in the world, then there is no darkness at all — for the essential light is only Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as it were, as above. And then: "night shall shine as day," etc. — as it is written: <span class="verse">"even the darkness is not dark to You, and night shines as the day; the darkness is as the light"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 139:12)</span> — as it shall be in the Future — as it is written: <span class="verse">"and at evening time there shall be light"</span> <span class="source">(Zechariah 14:7)</span> — as we ask [in the <i>Haggadah</i> of <i>Pesach</i>]: "Illuminate like the light of day the darkness of night." For the essential darkness of night is from the aspect of the wisdom of nature — which is the essential darkness. And <i>emunas hahashgachah</i> is the essential light, as above. And therefore, the night of the searching for <i>chametz</i> — the nullification of nature — the Tanna called "light" — in a refined expression — on account of the nullification of nature, which is the aspect of the <i>chametz</i> that one searches for on that night. Through which, the night is in the aspect of light — the aspect of: "night shall shine as day," etc. — as above. And therefore, the Tanna called that night "light."</p>

<span class="ois">§9</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">"a night of watching"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 12:42)</span> — which is <span class="key">guarded from the harmful spirits</span>. For the essential harmful spirits are from the aspect of the wisdom of nature — which is the aspect of <i>dinim</i> — which is the aspect of the idolatrous nations, the destroyers of the world. And then, on the night of the Exodus from Egypt — when there was the nullification of nature at night specifically — in order to break and nullify the aspect of night, which is the aspect of the wisdom of nature — therefore, that night is guarded from all the harmful spirits and from all the <i>dinim</i>. For then <i>hashgachah</i> was revealed — through which all damages and all <i>dinim</i> are nullified, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§10</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">fullness of the moon</span> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun, as the light of the seven days of Creation"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 30:26)</span> — etc. — which shall be in the Future, when His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i> is revealed in the world. For then the darkness of night shall be nullified, and the moon shall be filled from its diminishment. For the blemish and diminishment of the moon is the aspect of the darkness of night — which is the aspect of the wisdom of nature — which is the essential hold [of the <i>kelipos</i>]. For all their hold is from the aspect of the blemish of the moon, as is known. And in the Future, the moon shall be filled and the darkness shall be nullified — for nature shall be nullified and <i>hashgachah</i> shall be revealed — and then "night shall shine as day." And this is the aspect of: "And the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun," etc. — as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, the passage of <span class="key"><i>kiddush hachodesh</i></span> [the sanctification of the new month] is the first <i>mitzvah</i> that Israel was commanded in Egypt, at the time of the redemption. For the essential redemption — which is the nullification of nature — is the aspect of the fullness of the moon — which is the aspect of <i>kiddush hachodesh</i>, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§11</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="source">(Pesachim 5a)</span>: "The removal of <i>chametz</i> is only through <span class="key">burning</span>." For: <span class="verse">"from the fire they came forth, and the fire shall consume them"</span> <span class="source">(Ezekiel 15:7)</span>. For <i>hashgachah</i> and nature are the aspect of day and night, light and darkness, as above — and this is the aspect of <i>me'orai or</i> [luminaries of light] and <i>me'orai eish</i> [luminaries of fire]. For the luminaries of fire rule at the time of the departure of the luminaries of light — that is, at night and in darkness. For fire is the aspect of the intensity of <i>din</i> that is drawn from the aspect of nature, as above. And therefore, Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> created fire at the departure of <i>Shabbos</i> through Adam HaRishon, as our Sages said <span class="source">(Pesachim 54a)</span>. This is a hint to the aspect of nature, in which the <i>hashgachah</i> is concealed. For nature is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"my power and the might of my hand have made me"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 8:17)</span> — etc. — like fire, whose essential creation was through the work of man's hands. And therefore, from there is the essential hold of nature — which is the intensity of <i>din</i>. And therefore, we make <i>havdalah</i> over it at the departure of <i>Shabbos</i> — for there is the essential aspect of <i>havdalah</i> and clarification. For the essential hold of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil is from the aspect of nature, which is the aspect of fire, as above. And through our making <i>havdalah</i> over it — through this, we clarify the good and subdue the evil that clings to the fire, in the aspect of nature. And the fire too — which is the aspect of nature — is encompassed in holiness. For in truth, even nature is <i>hashgachah</i> — for Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> Himself conducts nature as He wills <i>yisbarach</i>. And when one believes and knows that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> and even nature is <i>hashgachah</i> — then the fire too is encompassed in holiness. And this is the aspect of: <i>"Borei me'orai ha'eish"</i> — that we bless at the departure of <i>Shabbos</i> during <i>havdalah</i> — that we believe that everything is from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, and even the fire — the aspect of nature — Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> Himself also created. For even nature is <i>hashgachah</i>, as above — and then everything is encompassed in holiness. And this is the aspect of the rectification of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil, as above.</p>

<p>And then, through this specifically, they fall — in the aspect of: "from the fire they came forth, and the fire shall consume them." For the essential hold [of the <i>kelipos</i>] is from the aspect of fire — the aspect of nature. And when it is revealed that even the fire — the aspect of nature — is from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> — through this itself they are subdued. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">removal of <i>chametz</i> through fire</span>. For then the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> is revealed — and then one knows that everything is from Him <i>yisbarach</i> — and even nature — the aspect of fire — Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> alone created everything. And then the <i>chametz</i> — the aspect of the wisdom of nature, the aspect of the hold of the nations — is subdued and nullified through its own root specifically — that is, through fire. For "from the fire they came forth, and the fire shall consume them," as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§12</span>

<p>And therefore, throughout the entire year, <i>chametz</i> is permitted — only on <i>Pesach</i> must one eat <i>matzah</i> and <i>chametz</i> is forbidden — and its prohibition is very stringent, even in the <span class="key">smallest amount</span>. For on <i>Pesach</i>, which is the Exodus from Egypt, one must eat only <i>matzah</i> — which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. And the aspect of <i>chametz</i> — which is the aspect of nature — must now be removed entirely, in <i>bal yeira'eh</i> and <i>bal yimatzei</i> [it shall not be seen and shall not be found]. For in truth, even nature itself is also the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, as above. But since Pharaoh and Egypt overpowered us greatly and denied Hashem, saying: <span class="verse">"Who is Hashem?"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 5:2)</span> — therefore, it was impossible to leave Egypt except through the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i> to a very, very great degree — as it was at the time of the Exodus from Egypt, when Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> revealed His <i>hashgachah</i> in the world in a very great revelation — for He performed awesome signs for us. And therefore, one must then, on <i>Pesach</i>, eat only <i>matzah</i> and not <i>chametz</i>, which is the aspect of nature — only <i>matzah</i>, which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. For on account of the intensity of the exile in Egypt — which encompasses all the exiles — it is impossible to leave from there except through the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i> alone. And the aspect of nature — which is the <i>chametz</i> — must be removed entirely, in <i>bal yeira'eh</i> and <i>bal yimatzei</i>. For through the aspect of nature, they would be able to overpower, and it would be impossible to leave on account of the greatness of their hold that they took upon Israel.</p>

<p>But since one eats <i>matzah</i> — which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — for seven days, then afterward <i>chametz</i> is permitted. For since we have already left Egypt and the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> has been revealed through eating <i>matzah</i> — then afterward one can eat <i>chametz</i> too — which is the aspect of nature — for through the greatness of the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i>, one knows the truth: that even nature is <i>hashgachah</i> — for Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> created everything and conducts everything as He wills. Therefore, one can eat <i>chametz</i> also. But at first, at the time of the Exodus from Egypt, it is impossible to eat <i>chametz</i> at all — for then, on account of the greatness of their hold, as above, it is forbidden to mention nature at all — lest they hold on more, and [Israel] would not be able to be redeemed, G-d forbid. But afterward, having already left them and the <i>hashgachah</i> having been revealed — then one knows that even the <i>chametz</i> — the aspect of nature — everything is through His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i>. And therefore, <i>chametz</i> is permitted after <i>Pesach</i>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what is written in the Holy <i>Zohar</i>: that since we have received the <i>matzah</i>, which is the <span class="aramaic"><i>asvasa</i></span> [remedy], we can afterward eat the <i>chametz</i>. That is, as above: after the <i>hashgachah</i> has been revealed, one can eat <i>chametz</i> too — for the <i>da'as</i> has been magnified and one knows that even nature is truly <i>hashgachah</i>, as above. And therefore, <i>chametz</i> was not permitted until after the <span class="key">splitting of the Sea of Reeds</span> — which was on the seventh day of <i>Pesach</i>. For then was the essential downfall of Egypt, and then there was even more and more revelation of <i>hashgachah</i>, to a very great degree, through the splitting of the Sea of Reeds and the many miracles that occurred then. And therefore, then the wisdom of nature was subdued and nullified — from which was the hold of the nations, greatly — for they were all terrified then greatly through the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i> that was then, to a great degree — as it is written: <span class="verse">"Then the chieftains of Edom were frightened"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 15:15)</span> — etc. And from the greatness of the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i> then, it was revealed that even in truth, nature is <i>hashgachah</i>. And therefore, after the seventh day of <i>Pesach</i>, <i>chametz</i> was permitted, etc. — as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§13</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">counting of the <i>Omer</i></span> — that we count from <i>Pesach</i> until <i>Shavuos</i>, forty-nine days — corresponding to the forty-nine gates of <i>Binah</i>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — from which is drawn all the <i>hashgachah</i>, all the <i>da'as</i>, all the nullification of nature, as above. And on <i>Shavuos</i>, the fiftieth day, is the <i>Giving of the Torah</i> — for the Torah is drawn from the fiftieth gate, as is known. For the Torah is the essential <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>. And therefore, it is counted forty-nine days from <i>Pesach</i> — from the time of the Exodus from Egypt, when the <i>hashgachah</i> began to be revealed — one counts each day until one draws upon oneself all the forty-nine gates of <i>Binah</i> — the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — until one merits on the fiftieth day to receive the Torah — which is drawn from the fiftieth gate. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And you shall count for yourselves from the day after the <i>Shabbos</i>"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 23:15)</span> — "from the day after the <i>Shabbos</i>" specifically — for <i>Pesach</i> is called <i>Shabbos</i>, as above — for all the miracles and the nullification of nature is drawn from the aspect of <i>Shabbos</i>, which is <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, as above. And from there one counts until <i>Shavuos</i>, the fiftieth day — corresponding to the fifty gates of <i>Binah</i>, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§14</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of the two tears that [the Holy One, blessed be He] drops into the Great Sea — as stated above in the discourse of our Rebbe mentioned above. For the tears are dropped into the Great Sea specifically — which is the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i> — the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — from which the <i>hashgachah</i> is drawn, as above. And the two tears are two drops of <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"for the earth shall be full of the <i>da'as</i> of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea"</span> — etc. — as above — that are drawn from <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — from the Great Sea — the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>, as above. And through this, Israel is saved from the exile — through the <i>hashgachah</i> that is drawn from the ends of the world, as above. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and their sound is heard from one end of the world to the other"</span> — for the <i>hashgachah</i> is drawn from the ends of the world, from <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§15</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key"><i>tevilas keilim</i></span> [immersion of vessels]. For the vessel that came from the possession of an idolater must be immersed in a <i>mikveh</i> so that it will be fit for a Jew to eat from it <span class="source">(Shulchan Aruch, Yoreh Dei'ah 120:1)</span>. For the idolaters — who are the aspect of nature — this is the essential <i>tumah</i>, as above. And when everything is in their possession, it cannot go out to the possession of Israel, to holiness, except through immersion in a <i>mikveh</i> — which is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>, the aspect of <i>da'as</i> — the aspect of: "for the earth shall be full of <i>da'as</i> like the waters," etc. — as above.</p>

<p>For the food of Israel must be in great holiness. And the essential sanctity of eating is through the <i>da'as</i> — which is the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i>. And this is the aspect of eating <i>matzah</i> on <i>Pesach</i> — that one reveals the <i>hashgachah</i> through the eating specifically — through eating <i>matzah</i>, as above. For Adam HaRishon blemished through the eating of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — and the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil is the aspect of the wisdom of nature, where good and evil are mixed. And it is the <i>da'as</i> of the <i>sitra achra</i> — the blemish of the <i>da'as</i> of holiness. And the essential blemish was through eating. For the essential rectification of eating is through <i>emunah</i> specifically — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and graze on <i>emunah</i>"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 37:3)</span> — as is brought in another place <span class="source">(Likutay Moharan I, 62)</span>. For when one does not eat in holiness, through this the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> is blemished, and one falls to the error of the wisdom of nature — as it is written: <span class="verse">"lest you eat and be sated… and your heart become haughty, and you forget Hashem your G-d… and say in your heart: 'My power and the might of my hand have made me this wealth'"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 8:12–17)</span> — etc. — that is, attributing things to nature, G-d forbid — as if one's livelihood comes through his own power and the might of his hand, not acknowledging <i>hashgachah</i>. And this is the aspect of "my power and the might of my hand" — the aspect of the blemish of the hands mentioned above — the blemish of the 28 joints of the hands — the 28 letters of the account of Creation.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">"And you shall remember Hashem your G-d, for He is the One Who gives you <i>koach</i> [power]"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 8:18)</span> — etc. — that is, in truth everything is through the <i>hashgachah</i> of Hashem <i>yisbarach</i>, Who created everything through the 28 [<i>koach</i> in gematria] letters of the account of Creation, as above. And He oversees at all times and gives <i>koach</i> — "28" specifically, as above. For Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> oversees and sustains the world through the 28 letters of the account of Creation, as above. And therefore, Israel must sanctify their food greatly. And this is the aspect of the many <i>mitzvos</i> that pertain to food and drink — for the essential revelation of <i>hashgachah</i> depends on the sanctity of food, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">"And you shall eat and be sated, and you shall bless Hashem your G-d for the good land"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 8:10)</span> — etc. — that is, you shall bless Hashem after eating — that you shall know that everything is from Him, through His <i>hashgachah</i> <i>yisbarach</i>. And this is: "for the good land" — for <i>Eretz Yisrael</i> is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — as it is written: <span class="verse">"the eyes of Hashem your G-d are always upon it"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 11:12)</span> — as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of eating the <span class="key"><i>manna</i></span> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Behold, I will rain down for you bread from heaven"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 16:4)</span> — which would descend through <i>hashgachah</i> alone — each day's portion on its day — and many miracles were performed through it. And when one believes that one's livelihood all comes from Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> through His <i>hashgachah</i> alone, without any way of nature at all — for He is the One Who gives <i>koach</i>, etc. — as above — this is the aspect of eating the <i>manna</i> — in the aspect of: "The Torah was only given to the eaters of the <i>manna</i>." And therefore, at the beginning of Israel's drawing close to their Father in Heaven — that is, on <i>Pesach</i>, at the time of the Exodus from Egypt — they must eat <i>matzah</i>, which is the aspect of <i>mochin</i> and <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>manna</i>. For through eating <i>matzah</i> on <i>Pesach</i>, great <i>da'as</i> is drawn and one knows that everything is through <i>hashgachah</i> alone. And through this is the essential drawing-close of Israel to their Father in Heaven, etc. — as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, the vessel that was in the possession of idolaters — who are from the <span class="aramaic"><i>sitra d'mesaavusa</i></span> [side of impurity] — for they attribute things to nature, from which is the essential hold of the <i>dinim</i> and the <i>sitra achra</i> — and therefore, the vessel is not fit for a Jewish meal except through immersion in a <i>mikveh</i>. Through which, the vessel goes from the aspect of nature to the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — which is the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>, etc. — as above. And this is the aspect of <span class="key"><i>hechsher keilim</i></span> [kashering of vessels]: <span class="verse">"Everything that comes through fire, you shall pass through fire"</span> <span class="source">(Numbers 31:23)</span> — for "from the fire they came forth, and the fire shall consume them," etc. — as above. For since the prohibition has already been absorbed in the vessel — all of which is drawn from the aspect of nature — that is, heresies, from which are drawn all the impurities and all the prohibitions — and since the prohibition has already been absorbed in the vessel, it has no purification except through fire — which is the aspect of the root of nature, etc. — as above. For "from the fire they came forth," etc. — as above. But when the prohibition has not yet been absorbed in the vessel — only that it went out from the possession of the idolater — that is, it went out from his <i>da'as</i> and possession (for the essential "possession" of a person is the <i>da'as</i>, through which he acquires all things under his control — in the aspect of: <span class="source">[Nedarim 41a]</span> "if you acquired <i>da'as</i>, what do you lack?" — etc. — for the essential person is the <i>da'as</i>) — and therefore, when the vessel goes out from the possession of the idolater — that is, from the dominion of the <i>da'as</i> of the idolater, which is the aspect of nature, etc. — as above — then it suffices to immerse it in a <i>mikveh</i> — which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, from which one receives and draws the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — to break and nullify the aspect of nature. Through which, one goes from <i>tumah</i> to <i>taharah</i>, from the possession of the idolater to the possession of Israel — who are above nature, etc. — as above.</p>

<span class="ois">§16</span>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">wine of the Four Cups</span>. For wine contains two aspects — as our Sages said <span class="source">(Yoma 76b)</span>: "If he merits — it makes him a head [<i>rosh</i>]; if he does not merit — it makes him a pauper [<i>rash</i>]." That is, when one merits, the <i>da'as</i> is elevated through the wine — and the essential <i>da'as</i> is the revelation of <i>hashgachah</i>. That is, the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> is revealed even more through the drinking of wine, when one merits — the aspect of: "if he merits, he becomes a head." But if he does not merit, it is the opposite — for "he becomes a pauper" — and there is no poverty except from <i>da'as</i>. And from there is the essential poverty in actuality — that is, when one lacks the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i>, which is the essential <i>da'as</i> — from there comes poverty — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"in sorrow you shall eat of it"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 3:17)</span> — which is the aspect of hardship and poverty that comes through the blemish of eating of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — which is the aspect of the wisdom of nature, as above.</p>

<p>For nature is the aspect of darkness and night, the aspect of the blemish of the moon, as above — from which is the essential poverty, as is known. And these two aspects are encompassed in wine — for wine brings sleep — and this is the aspect of nature, which is the aspect of night and sleep, as above. And conversely, when one merits, the wine awakens from sleep — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and your palate is like good wine — moving the lips of those who sleep"</span> <span class="source">(Song of Songs 7:10)</span>. That is, the good wine, from the side of good, awakens from sleep — which is the aspect of speech. For during sleep, speech departs — and through the good wine, one is awakened from sleep and speech is drawn, which comes from the <i>da'as</i>, as is known — the aspect of: "moving the lips of those who sleep." And this is the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i>, which is the aspect of awakening from sleep, as above.</p>

<p>And because wine is encompassed of the two aspects — the aspect of <i>da'as</i>, the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the aspect of joyful wine, the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and wine that gladdens"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 104:15)</span> — etc. — and this is when one merits, as above. And if he does not merit, it is the aspect of intoxicating wine, which confuses the <i>da'as</i> and errs in the wisdom of nature, G-d forbid — which is the aspect of sleep, etc. — as above. Therefore, one must <span class="key">guard the wine very much from the touch of idolaters</span> — more than anything else in the world. For nothing else becomes forbidden through the touch of an idolater — only wine becomes <i>nesech</i> [libation] through the touch of an idolater. For as soon as the idolater touches the wine — and ordinary touching is with the hands — then the wine is drawn to the aspect of nature — which is the aspect of the idolatrous nations of the world. Because the wine is encompassed of the two aspects, as above — therefore, the idolaters — who are the aspect of nature — can defile the wine through their touch with their hand — for it is immediately drawn to the aspect of nature. And therefore, it is not fit for Israel — who are above nature — and all their foods and beverages must be holy — that through the food and drink the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> should be drawn, as above. And therefore, the essential blemish of the wine is through their touch — and ordinary touch is with the hands — for the essential blemish of the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i> is through the blemish of the hands — the blemish of the 28 joints of the hands, which correspond to the 28 letters of the account of Creation, etc. — as above. And the hands of the idolaters are the opposite of this — and they are in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the hands are the hands of Eisav"</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 27:22)</span> — the aspect of the error of nature — which is the aspect of: "my power and the might of my hand," as above. And therefore, the wine is blemished through the idolaters, as above — and then it becomes <i>nesech</i>. This is the aspect of the error of the wisdom of nature — which is the aspect of sleep. And this is the aspect of <i>nesech</i> — the aspect of: <span class="verse">"for Hashem has poured [<i>nasach</i>] upon you a spirit of deep sleep"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 29:10)</span> — etc. — which is said there regarding the stargazers who err in the arrangement of the heavens, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, at the time of the redemption from Egypt — when the <i>hashgachah</i> was revealed — then it is a <i>mitzvah</i> to drink <span class="key">four cups of wine</span>. For then the wine is in the aspect of: "if he merits, he becomes a head." For now, on the night of <i>Pesach</i>, the <i>da'as</i> is elevated and the <i>hashgachah</i> is revealed even more through the wine. For Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> drew <i>hashgachah</i> and broke the night and sleep — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"At about midnight, I will go out in the midst of Egypt"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 11:4)</span>. And then the wine is the aspect of joyful wine — and one can speak and tell of the Exodus from Egypt on this night through the wine — in the aspect of: "moving the lips of those who sleep," as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="source">(Berachos 35a)</span>: "Song is said only over wine." For all the songs are drawn from the aspect of <span class="aramaic"><i>alma d'asei</i></span>, where song shall be aroused in the world — as is written in the Holy <i>Zohar</i> — in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Then Moshe will sing"</span> — "<i>sang</i>" is not stated, rather "<i>will sing</i>" — from here [we learn] that he is destined to sing in the World to Come. For the essential song is from the aspect of the World to Come, where Moshe will sing, etc. — for then, song shall be aroused in the world. And from there, all the songs are drawn to this world — that we sing and chant regarding the miracles. For all the miracles are performed through Hashem <i>yisbarach</i> drawing the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> from the ends of the world — from the World to Come — to this world, as above. And then, when the miracle is performed, we also draw the aspect of song from the World to Come to this world. And this is the aspect of all the songs of the miracles. And therefore, "song is said only over wine" — for then the wine is encompassed in holiness, in the aspect of the <i>da'as</i> of <i>hashgachah</i>. And this is the essential aspect of the song — that one draws the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — which is the aspect of the song of the miracle — to this world. And therefore, one says the song over wine, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key">four cups</span> of wine of <i>Pesach</i> — corresponding to the <span class="key">four kingdoms</span>. For when the wine is encompassed in holiness, in the aspect of <i>hashgachah</i> — through this, all the exiles of all the four kingdoms are subdued — whose essential power is through nature, as above. And through the <i>hashgachah</i> that is revealed through the <i>da'as</i> that is drawn through the cups of wine — through this, they are all nullified, etc. — as above.</p>

